ZIP picked up successfully
      ↓
Moved to in-process
      ↓
EPIC ZIP-to-PDF processing started
      ↓
ZIP entry processing error
(only DEFLATED entries supported/processed)
      ↓
No PDFs generated/extracted
      ↓
PolicyFilePath = null
      ↓
Valid PDF Count = 0
      ↓
No final PDF generated

⸻

Important Finding

The mock test confirms that the overall EPIC processing pipeline is being triggered correctly, including S3 pickup, file movement, temporary directory creation, and initiation of the EPIC conversion flow.

However, this test cannot be used as evidence that the mock PDF has the same PDF-content issue as the production PDF because the processing stopped before the PDF could reach the relevant conversion/merge stage.

Therefore, the mock test should be considered a partial reproduction/validation of the processing flow, rather than a complete reproduction of the production incident.

⸻

Next Validation

To continue the reproduction using the available mock data, the mock ZIP should be recreated using DEFLATED compression and submitted again through the DEV input bucket.

The objective of the second test is to allow the contained PDFs to reach the actual PDF conversion and merge stages.

The next test should specifically verify whether the application subsequently encounters the same type of PDF/Aspose processing error observed in production.

