One sentence I strongly recommend adding to the RCA

Due to production-data sensitivity, the original production ZIP/PDF could not be used for reproduction in DEV; therefore, a mock EOSMODEL ZIP was used for validation. The initial mock test did not reach the PDF conversion stage because of a ZIP compression-format issue, so it does not by itself establish the root cause of the production PDF failure.

This wording keeps the RCA technically accurate and prevents anyone reviewing it from asking, “If the mock failed, how do you know it is the same issue as production?”
